---
/**
 * Studio exhibit: Future Thesis OS.
 *
 * A static English snapshot of the project's own dashboard, taken on
 * 29 August 2026 and frozen. Nothing on the page runs, updates, or reaches the
 * network: the board reads a single `data.json` sitting next to it under
 * `public/studio/future-thesis-os/app/`.
 */
import StudioAppLayout from "../../layouts/StudioAppLayout.astro";

const description = "Turns scattered signals into testable views of technology and industry.";
---

<StudioAppLayout
  title="Future Thesis"
  description={description}
  appSrc="/studio/future-thesis-os/app/index.html"
  appTitle="Future Thesis map of trends, links, chains, and scenarios"
>
  <Fragment slot="intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">Studio</p>
    <h1>Future Thesis</h1>
    <p>
      Information is no longer scarce. News, papers, earnings, product releases, and technical
      writing arrive faster than any one person can connect them. The harder problem is deciding
      what the signals mean together, across fields and timescales, and knowing what evidence would
      change that view.
    </p>
    <p>
      Future Thesis is a personal world model for that task. It maintains trends, the mechanisms
      linking them, the paths those links form, and falsifiable scenarios about where they lead. A
      weekly cycle searches for evidence, updates probabilities, and records why a view moved,
      turning a stream of fragments into judgments that can be tested over time.
    </p>
    <a class="text-link" href="/studio/">Back to Studio</a>
  </Fragment>
</StudioAppLayout>
